          "_name": "article21",
          "_sourceTheme": "startm5",
          "_customHTML": "<section data-bs-version=\"5.1\" class=\"article021\" group=\"Article\" mbr-class=\"{'mbr-parallax-background': bg.parallax}\">\n    <mbr-parameters>\n        <header>Size</header>\n        <input type=\"checkbox\" title=\"Full Width\" name=\"fullWidth\">\n        <input type=\"checkbox\" name=\"reverseContent\" title=\"Reverse\">\n        <input type=\"range\" inline title=\"Top\" name=\"paddingTop\" min=\"0\" max=\"10\" step=\"1\" value=\"5\">\n        <input type=\"range\" inline title=\"Bottom\" name=\"paddingBottom\" min=\"0\" max=\"10\" step=\"1\" value=\"5\">\n        <header>Show/Hide</header>\n        <input type=\"checkbox\" title=\"Title\" name=\"showTitle\" checked>\n        <input type=\"checkbox\" title=\"Subtitle\" name=\"showSubtitle\" checked>\n        <input type=\"checkbox\" name=\"showButton\" title=\"Buttons\">\n        <header>Card</header>\n        <input type=\"color\" title=\"Card BG\" name=\"cardbg\" value=\"#ffffff\" selected>\n        <input type=\"color\" title=\"Card Color\" name=\"cardbg\" value=\"#ff8f7a\" selected>\n        <input type=\"color\" title=\"Icon Color\" name=\"iconColor\" value=\"#550000\" selected>\n        <header>Background</header>\n        <fieldset type=\"background\" name=\"bg\" parallax>\n            <input type=\"image\" title=\"Image\" value=\"@PROJECT_PATH@/assets/images/img-395-646x431.jpg\">\n            <input type=\"color\" title=\"Color\" value=\"#550000\" selected>\n            <input type=\"video\" title=\"Video\" value=\"https://vimeo.com/428046504\">\n        </fieldset>\n        <header condition=\"bg.type === 'video'\">Fallback Image</header>\n        <input type=\"image\" title=\"Fallback Image\" value=\"../_images/background1.jpg\" name=\"fallBackImage\" condition=\"bg.type === 'video'\">\n        <input type=\"checkbox\" title=\"Overlay\" name=\"overlay\" condition=\"bg.type !== 'color'\" checked>\n        <input type=\"color\" title=\"Overlay Color\" name=\"overlayColor\" value=\"#000000\" condition=\"overlay && bg.type !== 'color'\">\n        <input type=\"range\" inline title=\"Opacity\" name=\"overlayOpacity\" min=\"0\" max=\"1\" step=\"0.1\" value=\"1\" condition=\"overlay && bg.type !== 'color'\">\n    </mbr-parameters>\n    <div mbr-class=\"{'container': !fullWidth, 'container-fluid': fullWidth}\">\n        <div class=\"row justify-content-center\">\n            <div class=\"col-lg-4\">\n                <div class=\"col-12 col-md-12\">\n                    <h5 class=\"mbr-section-title mbr-fonts-style mt-0 mb-4\" mbr-if=\"showTitle\" data-app-selector=\".mbr-section-title\" mbr-theme-style=\"display-2\">\n                        <b>Join our community</b>\n                    </h5>\n                    <h6 class=\"mbr-section-subtitle mbr-fonts-style mt-0 mb-4\" mbr-if=\"showSubtitle\" data-app-selector=\".mbr-section-subtitle, .main-button\" mbr-theme-style=\"display-7\">ZIFF is a student-led film festival with a bigger purpose: bringing young people together through film while supporting the preservation of Roșia Montană’s heritage. We’re looking for enthusiastic young people from different schools who would like to get involved, learn new skills and help make the festival happen.<div>Whether you’re interested in film, media, event organisation, fundraising, design or simply want to be part of a team working on something meaningful, there’s a place for you at ZIFF.</div><div>By joining us, you’ll help create a festival for young filmmakers and audiences while supporting the “Adoptă o Casă” programme and the people working to preserve Roșia Montană’s unique historic buildings and traditions.</div><div>Join the team!</div></h6>\n                    <div class=\"mbr-section-btn item-footer mt-3  main-button\" mbr-if=\"showButton\" data-toolbar=\"-mbrBtnMove,-mbrBtnAdd\" mbr-buttons mbr-theme-style=\"display-7\">\n                        <a href class=\"btn item-btn btn-primary\" data-app-placeholder=\"Type Text\">\n                            Learn more\n                        </a>\n                    </div>\n                </div>\n            </div>\n\n            <div class=\"col-lg-8 side-features\">\n                <div class=\"item-wrapper align-left\">\n                    <div class=\"counter-container mbr-text mbr-fonts-style\" mbr-theme-style=\"display-7\" data-app-selector=\".mbr-text\" data-multiline mbr-article>\n                        <div><b>Tech &amp; Logistics Department</b></div><div><i><u>Ensuring the digital infrastructure is reliable and the physical event runs smoothly.</u></i></div><div><i><u>All roles are based in Bucharest</u></i></div><div><br></div><div><u>IT (Information Technology) - one position available</u></div><div>Role Description:</div><div>The IT team manages ZIFF's digital systems, including the website, ticketing integration, screening portals, and on-site network stability.</div><div>Key Responsibilities:</div><div>- Maintain and update the official website (zoomin-filmfest.com) for a seamless user experience.</div><div>- Oversee digital ticketing platforms, pass validation, and screening scheduling systems.</div><div>- Set up secure, high-speed networks and tech kiosks at physical venues.</div><div>- Provide real-time troubleshooting for live-streamed Q&amp;As and hybrid screenings. - I think it s too vague, i would just let it at realt time troubleshooting</div><div><u><br></u></div><div><u>Logistics - two positions available</u>&nbsp;</div><div>Role Description:</div><div>The logistics manager coordinates venues, projection equipment, schedules, and transport for assets and VIP guests.</div><div>Key Responsibilities:</div><div>- Coordinate film traffic so digital prints, DCPs, and projection files arrive safely and are tested on-site.</div><div>- Manage room setups, seating capacities, and hardware delivery for panels and workshops.</div><div>- Plan accommodation for filmmakers arriving from outside of Bucharest.</div><div><br></div><div><b>Public Relations, Sponsorships &amp; Media Department</b></div><div><i><u>Safeguarding the ZIFF brand, driving registrations and ticket sales, and securing vital funding.</u></i></div><div><br></div><div><u style=\"font-size: 1rem;\">PR (Public Relations) - 3 positions available</u><br></div><div>Role Description:</div><div>PR manages the public voice of ZIFF through media relations, press visibility, Gala Night coverage and post-event coverage.</div><div>Key Responsibilities:</div><div>- Write and distribute social media posts (two/week), press releases (a minimum of three) to local media.</div><div>- Pitch festival highlights and filmmakers</div><div>- Coordinate Gala Night press access, creator interviews.</div><div>- Liaise with the Article Writer</div><div><u><br></u></div><div><u>Sponsorships - 2 positions available</u></div><div>Role Description:</div><div>The Sponsorships team builds and manages partnerships that support the festival financially and strategically.</div><div>Key Responsibilities:</div><div>- Identify, pitch, and secure local businesses and national brands.</div><div>- Liaise with the Media, Advertising and Marketing Department to deliver all sponsor benefits, including logo placement, program ads, and Gala Night recognition.</div><div>- Draft sponsorship contracts in a way that is mutually beneficial.</div><div>- Maintain strong partner relationships to support future multi-year collaborations.</div><div><br></div><div><b>Editorial &amp; Content Creation</b></div><div><i style><u style>Documenting the festival story and keeping the community informed</u></i></div><div><br></div><div><u>Article Writer - 2 positions available</u>&nbsp;</div><div>Role Description:</div><div>The Article Writer creates editorial content that brings ZIFF to life online and in festival communications.</div><div>Key Responsibilities:</div><div>- Write blog pieces such as film spotlights, watchlists, and feature stories (one/week)</div><div>- Conduct written or transcribed Q&amp;As with filmmakers and industry guests (one/day of the festival week)</div><div>- Produce the recap and program-guide blurbs for selected films one week before the festival.</div><div><br></div><div><u>Media, Advertising &amp; Marketing - 3 positions available \n</u></div><div><span style=\"font-size: 1rem;\">Role Description:</span><br></div><div>This team drives audience growth through campaigns, design assets, and social content.\n</div><div>Key Responsibilities:\n</div><div>- Design, launch, and monitor digital ads (social media - twice weekly) plus physical banners and posters.\n</div><div>- Create social campaigns featuring trailers, daily recap reels, and behind-the-scenes content (twice weekly).\n</div><div>- Analyze demographics and ticket metrics to optimize ad performance and ROI.</div><div><br></div><div><b>Finance &amp; Administration Department</b></div><div><i style><u>Keeping the organization compliant, secure, and financially healthy.</u></i></div><div>Finance Manager - one position available</div><div>Role Description:</div><div>The Finance department manages budgets, cash flow, and reporting to keep ZIFF financially responsible and efficient.</div><div>Key Responsibilities:</div><div>- Manage the master budget across festival branches (Logistics, Media, Hospitality).</div><div>- Handle cash flow, box office receipts, merchandise sales, and invoice payments.</div><div>- Process submission fee revenue, vendor payments, and post-festival financial reports.</div><div><br></div><div><b>People &amp; On-Site Leadership</b></div><div><i><u>The operational engine behind staffing, volunteer coordination, and venue execution.</u></i></div><div><br></div><div><u>Operations Supervisor - one position available</u></div><div>Role Description:</div><div>The Operations Supervisor leads on-site execution, resolves live issues quickly, and ensures a strong guest experience.</div><div>Key Responsibilities:</div><div>- Manage venue flow, so screenings begin on time and queues move efficiently.</div><div>- Serve as escalation point for live issues (ticket errors, missing equipment, VIP seating disputes).</div><div>- Coordinate daily with Logistics, IT, and Staffing to adjust resources in high-traffic areas.</div><div><b><br></b></div><div>\n</div><div>\n</div><div>\n</div><div>\n</div><div>\n</div><div>\n</div><div>\n</div><div>\n</div><div>\n</div><div>\n</div><div>\n</div><div>\n</div><div>\n</div>\n                    </div>\n                </div>\n            </div>\n        </div>\n    </div>\n</section>",
